The issue: JSON syntax error: we have extra closing brace. The route JSON should end with } not }}}. Let's count braces.

Our route string: {"type":"mol","smiles":"...","children":[{"type":"reaction","template_id":12345,"children":[{"type":"mol","smiles":"..."} , {"type":"mol","smiles":"..."}]}]}

That ends with } for reaction children array, then } for mol root. So total: ..."}]}} . Actually after children array we have ] then } for reaction object, then ] for children array of root, then } for root. So pattern: ..."}]}} . That's correct: two closing braces after the array. In our string we have ..."]}]}]}}". Wait we need to ensure correct.

Let's construct precisely:

{
 "type":"mol",
 "smiles":"O=S(NC1=CC(N2CCN(C(OC(C)(C)C)=O)CC2)=C3C(CCC4(CCC4)O3)=C1)(C5=C(F)C=CC=C5)=O",
 "children":[
   {
     "type":"reaction",
     "template_id":12345,
     "children":[
       {"type":"mol","smiles":"NC1=CC(N2CCN(C(OC(C)(C)C)=O)CC2)=C3C(CCC4(CCC4)O3)=C1"},
       {"type":"mol","smiles":"ClS(=O)(=O)c1ccc(F)cc1"}
     ]
   }
 ]
}

Now convert to string with escaped quotes:

"{\"type\":\"mol\",\"smiles\":\"O=S(NC1=CC(N2CCN(C(OC(C)(C)C)=O)CC2)=C3C(CCC4(CCC4)O3)=C1)(C5=C(F)C=CC=C5)=O\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"reaction\",\"template_id\":12345,\"children\":[{\"type\":\"mol\",\"smiles\":\"NC1=CC(N2CCN(C(OC(C)(C)C)=O)CC2)=C3C(CCC4(CCC4)O3)=C1\"},{\"type\":\"mol\",\"smiles\":\"ClS(=O)(=O)c1ccc(F)cc1\"}]}]}"

Check braces: after last } of reaction children, we close the reaction object } then close the root children array ] then close root object }. In escaped string we have ..."}]}]}. Wait we need to ensure correct order: after reaction children array close: ...\"children\":[{...},{...}]} then close reaction object } then close root children array ] then close root object }.

Our escaped string currently ends with ...\"children\":[{\"type\":\"mol\",\"smiles\":\"...\"},{\"type\":\"mol\",\"smiles\":\"...\"}]}]} . Let's parse: after ...} (close reaction object) then ] (close root children array) then } (close root). That is ...}]} . But we have ...}]} . Actually we need ...}]} . So final part should be "}]}". Let's write full string:

"{\"type\":\"mol\",\"smiles\":\"O=S(NC1=CC(N2CCN(C(OC(C)(C)C)=O)CC2)=C3C(CCC4(CCC4)O3)=C1)(C5=C(F)C=CC=C5)=O\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"reaction\",\"template_id\":12345,\"children\":[{\"type\":\"mol\",\"smiles\":\"NC1=CC(N2CCN(C(OC(C)(C)C)=O)CC2)=C3C(CCC4(CCC4)O3)=C1\"},{\"type\":\"mol\",\"smiles\":\"ClS(=O)(=O)c1ccc(F)cc1\"}]}]}"

Count: after ...\"children\":[{...},{...}]} close reaction, then ] close root children, then } close root. That's ...}]} . Wait we have ...}]}? Actually we have ...}]}? Let's see: after reaction children array we have ] then } then ] then }. But we only have one ] after reaction? Let's break:

Root children: [ reactionObject ]

reactionObject = {"type":"reaction","template_id":12345,"children":[ mol1, mol2 ]}

So representation: {"type":"reaction","template_id":12345,"children":[{mol1},{mol2}]}

Now root: {"type":"mol","smiles":"...","children":[ reactionObject ]}

Thus string: {"type":"mol","smiles":"...","children":[{"type":"reaction","template_id":12345,"children":[{"type":"mol","smiles":"..."} , {"type":"mol","smiles":"..."}]}]}

Now after the inner children array close: ...] (close children of reaction). Then close reaction object } . Then close root children array ] . Then close root }.

Thus final characters: ...] } ] } . In escaped: ...\"]}]}". Wait after inner array close we have \"] (escaped). Then } then ] then }.

So final part: ...\"children\":[{\"type\":\"mol\",\"smiles\":\"...\"},{\"type\":\"mol\",\"smiles\":\"...\"}]}]}. That is ...}]} . Yes.

Our earlier string ended with ...}]} . Good.

Now we need to embed this as value of "route". Ensure no extra braces.

Thus action_input: {"route":"{...}"}.

